{"parentUuid":"a5c0383d-90e2-4f2a-932d-6841a9b66063","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6e1af180-8c3d-4a38-afa9-78985af48754","agentId":"a0d8d847e1065c5ed","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013tVUNeLF8yh2SAtQmV4b4u","type":"tool_result","content":"research_notes/morphometry/README.md:211:- The shadow of each vertebra, sampled here as nanoDRR samples a ray (500 points from the source to the detector, each the label of its nearest voxel), equals FleXray's support of that label, where its channel is above zero, pixel for pixel in all nine views and levels.\nresearch_notes/morphometry/README.md:218:The shapes beside the straight lines are morphoview/shapes.py, each in the world's millimetres and each projected by the same camera: curves, open or closed, which project exactly, since a straight segment of the world is straight on the render, and are cut where they pass behind the source; arcs, circles, ellipses and centripetal splines sampled to 0.05 mm of the true curve; planes, fitted to points by least squares with their residual, with the angle between two, where a line meets one and the angle the render sees one at, and their patches; flat polygons; and volumes, whose projection is the length each ray runs through them, by a fine sampling that is the chord through their voxels or by FleXray's own, and their silhouettes. tests/test_shapes.py holds each to its geometry: the curves to their tolerance, a spline to the centripetal spans written again in Hermite form, a circle seen through parallel rays to the ellipse's area to 1e-4, a fitted plane to its points, a ball's path lengths to its chords and their sum to its volume to 0.005, and FleXray's sampling to nanoDRR's counted point by point.\nresearch_notes/morphometry/README.md:220:On the phantom the command takes 2 to 4 s a view with the mask, most of it the shadows (0.3 to 0.6 s a level); the 46 tests take about a minute (`python -m unittest morphoview.tests.test_projection morphoview.tests.test_shapes`), and Live, where FleXray and torch are installed, renders the views again.\nmorphoview/shapes.py:9:projects exactly, and a smooth curve within its tolerance times the magnification. A segment that\nmorphoview/shapes.py:15:patch is a flat polygon, a rectangle about the point unless corners are given, and a flat polygon","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"a8a20eee-74d4-4cd5-8b92-5ad712b39386","timestamp":"2026-10-30T18:48:07.131Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"ffaceb39-57f7-462a-ab76-a2603387696d","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/user/bordercall","root":"/home/user/bordercall","branch":"claude/project-thread-gv744i","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":3,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":6},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"OpenSpineConsortium/bordercall","visibility":"unknown"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"OpenSpineConsortium/bordercall","visibility":"unknown"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"OpenSpineConsortium/symphony-template","visibility":"unknown"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"OpenSpineConsortium/bordercall","visibility":"unknown"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"OpenSpineConsortium/SchwingNet","visibility":"unknown"}]}},"live_cwd":"/home/user/bordercall","platform":"linux"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a5c0383d-90e2-4f2a-932d-6841a9b66063","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_projects","cwd":"/home/user/bordercall","sessionId":"cbdcd57f-bcf8-5a71-ab64-4f0b9fbdb74f","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"zany-kindling-liskov"}
